                        "sense_id": "d3726cb5-25a2-31c7-9df6-b27e72a08f33",
                        "entry_id": "080f0c39-13fb-3eab-aad4-d8671244c58c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Pensivement."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e01478f3-5c6f-4af7-bf14-e238d2e9a100",
                                "sense_id": "d3726cb5-25a2-31c7-9df6-b27e72a08f33",
                                "text": "It seemed as though he went thoughtfully away to seek beyond the bounds of life which is apparent, the cause, the explanation, or the excuse for them.",
                                "translation": "Il semblait que, pensif, il en allât chercher, au delà de la vie apparente la cause, l’explication ou l’excuse. — (Victor Hugo, Les Misérables, 1862, traduction anglaise de Isabel F. Hapgood)"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "db4d012f-5287-306b-9bad-b6497c159fd4",
                        "entry_id": "080f0c39-13fb-3eab-aad4-d8671244c58c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Intelligemment, avec considération, avec réflexion, de manière réfléchie."
